these paris airport workers say that  they're overworked and overwhelmed and  they're on strike to demand better pay  and working conditions  it's a vicious circle the bosses cut  staff during the pandemic but salaries  are so low that they're unable to  recruit people so staff now have to cope  with more work as people travel again  it's causing a lot of stress  many workers say they've not had a pay  rise for years and with inflation  they're struggling financially sonya has  worked at ali airport for more than two  decades she says she's been forced to  resort to using food stamps to feed her  children  with inflation being so high in france  petrol is expensive it's just not  possible i can't afford to feed my kids  i can't fill my car i can't take my kids  on a break it's not normal because of  the strike paris airport authorities  have had to cancel one in six flights  for some travellers the reduced flights  mean disruption and longer queues  we came here four hours early as we knew  there was going to be a strike so we  were prepared  on tv i saw that there was an airport  workers strike so i called the airline  as i was worried they'd cancel the  flight but it's okay for now  the protesters say that if their demands  are not met they'll continue their  strike over the next few days as  france's school summer break begins many  people are going on holiday these  workers say they wish they could afford  to do the same natasha butler al jazeera  paris
 

